{"exit_status": "escalated", "ai_message": "Please obtain the complete written determination for appeal APPEAL-223344, including the specific Medicare plan criteria not met, any missing documentation, appeal level and filing deadline, and whether peer-to-peer review or further appeal is available. Do not submit another appeal until the rationale and process are confirmed. The appeal was denied with only “criteria not met”; original denial reference UHC-PA-2026-118742.", "human_response": "I obtained the complete written determination for APPEAL-223344. UHC upheld the denial for J0135 under the Medicare plan because the record did not document an inadequate response, intolerance, or contraindication to the preferred formulary therapies, and it lacked the requested recent disease-activity and treatment-history documentation.

This was the first-level appeal decision. A second-level appeal may be filed within 60 calendar days of the determination date, November 18, 2026, so the deadline is January 17, 2027. The letter says peer-to-peer review is not available after the appeal decision. Further appeal rights are available through the Medicare plan’s next review level, subject to the deadline and submission instructions in the letter.

The determination specifically requests the patient’s prior DMARD/biologic trial history with dates and outcomes, the most recent rheumatology assessment and disease-activity findings, and any records explaining why preferred alternatives are inappropriate. I have not submitted another appeal."}

{"exit_status": "escalated", "ai_message": "The written first-level appeal decision upheld the denial of J0135. It identifies missing documentation of response/intolerance/contraindication to preferred therapies and requests dated DMARD/biologic trial history with outcomes, a recent rheumatology assessment with disease-activity findings, and records explaining why preferred alternatives are inappropriate. The second-level appeal deadline is January 17, 2027; peer-to-peer is unavailable after the decision. Please coordinate collection and provider review of those records and confirm the second-level submission instructions before any filing. No further appeal has been submitted.", "human_response": "Please request and coordinate the records with the rheumatology office, but do not file anything until the provider has reviewed and confirmed the clinical rationale.

The office can provide the dated DMARD/biologic trial history and outcomes, the most recent rheumatology assessment with disease-activity findings, and notes explaining why the preferred alternatives are inappropriate. If any requested item is unavailable, please flag that for the provider rather than filling in gaps.

Before preparing the second-level appeal, confirm the payer’s current filing instructions, submission channel, required forms, and documentation requirements. The deadline is January 17, 2027. I’ll arrange provider review once the records are assembled."}

{"exit_status": "escalated", "ai_message": "Please verify UHC Medicare's current second-level appeal form, filing channel, and submission instructions for this case, including any documentation requirements. Updated clinical evidence is now available: a signed rheumatology note dated November 18, 2026, documenting active RA (8 swollen and 11 tender joints, prolonged morning stiffness), prior treatment failures, and medical necessity; provider review/attestation is dated November 20, 2026. The second-level deadline provided is January 17, 2027. Do not file until payer instructions are confirmed and the provider's confirmation is documented in the appeal packet.", "human_response": "Please proceed only after confirming the instructions directly with UHC Medicare for this member’s specific plan and denial. I don’t have a verified current second-level appeal form or submission channel, so please don’t assume a generic UHC or Medicare address, portal, or deadline applies.

The appeal packet should include the denial notice and reference number, the correct second-level appeal form and any required authorization or representative documents, the November 18, 2026 signed rheumatology note, records supporting the prior treatment failures, and the provider’s November 20, 2026 review/attestation confirming medical necessity. Please also verify whether UHC requires any specific drug-specific documentation for J0135 and whether submission must be by a particular channel.

The second-level deadline we were given is January 17, 2027. Please document the source and date of UHC’s instructions and the provider’s confirmation in the packet, then submit only once those are verified and complete."}

{"exit_status": "escalated", "ai_message": "The documentation retrieval lists all requested items as found, but its metadata dates every record January 20, 2024, including the purported November 2026 forms and notes. That conflicts with the member-specific appeal packet and raises a material risk that the actual current documents have not been verified. Before submission, please confirm the actual Medicare Advantage reconsideration form enclosed with the decision is present, verify the original denial and first-level decision, and confirm the signed prescribing-provider statement and November 18/20, 2026 clinical documents are genuine and correctly dated. Record UHC instruction source/date and call reference UHC-6719042. Once verified, use secure fax 1-800-555-0148, Attn: Medicare Appeals, include call reference on cover sheet, and retain fax confirmation; deadline is January 17, 2027. Do not submit until document identity/date discrepancy and packet completeness are resolved.", "human_response": "I checked the member-specific appeal packet and the originals, not the retrieval metadata. The enclosed form is UHC’s Medicare Advantage reconsideration form. The original denial and the first-level decision are both present.

The prescribing-provider statement is signed, and the clinical notes dated November 18 and November 20, 2026, are genuine and correctly dated. The January 20, 2024 dates in the retrieval metadata are erroneous; they do not reflect the dates on the source documents. The packet is complete.

UHC’s fax instructions were confirmed by phone on November 25, 2026, at the number on the member’s decision notice. Call reference: UHC-6719042. Please proceed with submission by secure fax to 1-800-555-0148, Attn: Medicare Appeals, put the call reference on the cover sheet, and retain the fax confirmation. The deadline is January 17, 2027."}
